# Fathom — UI: menus, game states, and the HUD

This file defines the game's screens — the menus and the state machine that moves
between them — and the heads-up display shown during a dive. The controls that drive
each screen are defined in `specs/movement.md`; scoring, lives, and depth (the values
the HUD shows) are in `specs/progression.md`.

## Menus and navigation

The main menu is a single dive: it lists `DIVE` (begin a dive), then `HOW TO PLAY`.
The selected item is highlighted, and the menu controls in `specs/movement.md` move
the selection and confirm it. Every menu and navigation path this specification
mandates must be present, rendered in the palette and monospace type
`specs/overview.md` defines.

## Game states

The game is a small state machine. Each state has a clear screen and controls
(controls are defined in `specs/movement.md`).

1. Title / main menu. Shows the title `FATHOM`, the tagline `HUNT IN THE DARK`, and a
   vertical menu with `DIVE` (begin a dive), followed by `HOW TO PLAY`. The selected
   item is highlighted. A dim, dark slice of maze may show behind the menu for
   atmosphere.
2. How to play. Describes the controls, the three predators and the signal each hunts,
   and the light-versus-sonar sensing. Returns to the menu.
3. In the maze. The live game: the dark maze, the forager and its light, the sonar and
   ink, plankton, predators where revealed, and the HUD.
4. Dive countdown. The brief pre-start hold at the top of a maze and after losing a
   life (a short `DIVE` countdown rendered over the maze view) before control
   resumes.
5. Paused. Reachable from live play. Offers Resume, Restart, and Quit to menu. The
   maze is visible but frozen behind the pause menu.
6. Maze cleared. A brief interstitial when a maze is cleared (for example
   `DEPTH 1 CLEARED`) before the next, deeper maze begins.
7. Game over. Shown when the last life is lost. Displays the final score and the depth
   reached, with `PLAY AGAIN` and `MENU`.

The three canonical screens — the title screen, the in-maze view, and the game-over
screen — must be implemented as described, in the palette and type `specs/overview.md`
defines.

## The HUD

The HUD occupies the strips above and below the maze region (see the coordinate
system in `specs/overview.md`); it is always fully lit and never fogged.

- Top strip (`y` in `[0, 80]`): the current score in large monospace digits (about
  `48 px` tall) toward the left, and a small dim mode label reading `{{#if (eq variant.slug "kindle")}}KINDLE{{else}}STANDARD{{/if}}` (the
  dive name) in the top-right corner.
- Bottom strip (`y` in `[656, 720]`): the remaining lives shown as small forager
  icons toward the left; the current depth (for example `DEPTH 1`) toward the right;
  and, between them, the sonar and ink readiness indicators, small gauges that fill
  back up as each ability comes off cooldown (the sonar pulse and ink are defined in
  `specs/gameplay.md`), so the player can see at a glance when each is ready.
